# How a lesson becomes a page. Coordinates are chosen by eye and mean nothing except that
# the written things are at the top and the produced things are at the bottom.

title How a lesson becomes a page
size 980 640

box src   40  60 260 110 "lesson.cs" "one program, with named" "regions in it called blocks"
box prose 330 60 300 110 "lesson.src.md" "prose with holes in it, where" "the code and the output go"
box gates 660 60 280 110 "gates.json" "the question asked before" "the answer is shown"

box  tool 320 250 340 90 "xray build" "runs the program once, then cuts" "the output at the markers"
note chk   40 250 240 90 "xray check" "the same code, one flag," "fails on a stale file"

box out1  40 430 260 100 "expected/*.txt" "what each block printed," "one file per block"
box out2 330 430 300 100 "lesson.md" "the page a reader opens" "and never edits"
box out3 660 430 280 100 "diagram.svg" "the picture, generated" "from a .dg file"

note foot 40 555 900 44 "The top row is written by a person. The bottom row is produced. No file is both."

arrow src tool
arrow prose tool
arrow gates tool
arrow tool out1
arrow tool out2
arrow tool out3
